  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Overlap along the board",
  "description": "Two queues, A and B, just inside the centre line. Goalkeeper in goal. A has the ball.\n\nA carries the ball diagonally out towards the board. Almost at the same time B sets off at high speed, skates behind A and up the outside along the board. When B is level with A, A plays the ball diagonally forward towards the board. B takes it at full speed, cuts in towards goal and shoots. A keeps the speed down during the overlap and then heads for the far post for a rebound.\n\nSwap queues after each go and run it from both sides. Progression: a defender stands in the way and has to choose between A and B, making it 2v1. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "B comes behind and outside A – never in front."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Play the ball when B is level with A, diagonally forward so B can take it at full speed."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "A slows down and draws the defence; speed is B's advantage."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "B brings the ball off the board and angles in towards goal before the shot."
    }
  ],
